+
+### Enhanced ground at the horizon
+
+- `pass/numos/numos_ground.slangh` owns the sphere intersection and the pinned ground
+  lighting without camera extinction. The composite, rainbow and PSR resolver use this
+  surface for hazed misses. The G-buffer and composite binding indices, resource
+  manager and `rtx_numos.cpp` carry both reflected-ground records to the post-depth air.
diff --git a/documentation/NumosSky.md b/documentation/NumosSky.md
index 2dea074c0..02ff6637a 100644
--- a/documentation/NumosSky.md
+++ b/documentation/NumosSky.md
@@ -181,3 +181,19 @@ preset, select Custom settings and turn off Follow game weather.
 The present thread requests a copy of the render thread's effective weather and diagnostics while a sky
 page is open. Menu edits use deferred RTX option writes. The game can apply its weather and look again
 on a map start or a change of weather.
+
+## Below the horizon
+
+With Enhanced haze active a miss into the planet ends on its Lambertian ground. The
+sphere uses the sky's camera altitude, with cloud shadows evaluated in the cloud frame.
+The near root in sky kilometres is converted back to host units. The air then converts
+that distance using its own units per kilometre, so changing Haze World Scale changes
+the air traversed without moving the ground. Both sides of a partially covered pixel
+are shaded before blending across one traced pixel.
+
+The camera samples the regular finite-surface haze and screen clouds. For a reflected
+or transmitted sky miss, the G-buffer saves its final segment's origin, direction,
+distance and coloured throughput separately for each compacted path. After depth the
+composite integrates that segment through the current air cache, adds the lit ground
+and the cloud dome, and applies the camera-to-mirror air. With haze off the ordinary
+NUMOS sky is used. Indirect sky lighting keeps the library's own ground.
